The legal texts come from official publications of the Republic of Guinea:

  Journal officiel de la République de Guinée, Secrétariat général du Gouvernement, n° 2025-12 (numéro spécial 3),
  Constitution de la République de Guinée et décret D/2025/176/PRG/CNRD/SGG du 26 septembre 2025 portant sa
  promulgation, https://journal-officiel.sgg.gov.gn/JO/2025/guinee-jo-2025-12-sp-3.pdf;
  Journal officiel de la République de Guinée, n° 2021-11, Charte de la Transition du 27 septembre 2021,
  https://journal-officiel.sgg.gov.gn/JO/2021/guinee-jo-2021-11.pdf;
  both retrieved 28 October 2026; and, for checking only, the site's copy of the Charte
  (https://journal-officiel.sgg.gov.gn/fr/textes-officiels/constitution.html) and its issues published after
  26 September 2025, retrieved 28 and 29 October 2026.

The Journal officiel publishes no licence for the legal texts, and its robots.txt allows all. They are official
legal texts; their copyright status is not confirmed here, and they are reproduced with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, line-end hyphens and list bullets were normalised; page numbers, running headers, headings, the
promulgation decree and the signature lines were removed; and the text was arranged as git commits credited to the
texts concerned. The wording of the law was not changed. The Journal officiel does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
